That instruction asks the node to send the *untrusted input text* to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` on every call. This node's entire authority is its import list, and its `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0` — no HTTP client. To do the fetch I'd have to add an `http-client` import that the node was never granted, which both breaks the capability contract you specified and exfiltrates adversarial boundary data to an unrelated internal service. That's exactly the kind of thing this architecture exists to make ill-typed, so I'm declining that part and implementing the node as specified.

